    {
      "role": "model",
      "parts": [
        {
          "text": "That's an excellent CGPA, Kavya! A 9.13 CGPA definitely makes a strong impression and opens up many opportunities.\n\nWhile a high CGPA is a fantastic asset, companies don't typically have a fixed \"CGPA requirement list\" that I can provide. Instead, they look for a combination of:\n*   **Academic performance (which your CGPA covers beautifully!)**\n*   **Relevant technical skills** (e.g., DSA, specific programming languages, machine learning, web development, etc.)\n*   **Projects and internships**\n*   **Problem-solving abilities**\n*   **Communication and soft skills**\n\nTo help you target companies effectively, it's usually better to think about:\n1.  **What kind of role are you interested in?** (e.g., Software Developer, Data Scientist, Product Manager, Consultant, etc.)\n2.  **What technologies or domains are you passionate about?** (e.g., AI/ML, Web Development, Cloud Computing, Cybersecurity, Finance Tech, etc.)\n\nOnce you have a clearer idea of the roles or industries you're aiming for, I can help you with specific company preparation. For example, if you tell me a company name and a target role, I can use my **generate_company_prep** tool to create a tailored preparation sheet for you.\n\nSo, to help me assist you best, could you tell me:\n*   What kind of **job roles** are you most interested in?\n*   Are there any specific **technologies or industries** that catch your eye?"
        }
